From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ams: AD5X IFS shows what Kiln's IFS driver is doing

Kiln OS's IFS driver says which operation runs (operation: load,
unload, swap, refill, eject, prefeed, feed, retract, select, tune), its
phase (heating, cutting, unloading, homing, selecting, feeding, purging,
priming), the slot it heads for (target_channel) and the slot moving
now (activity_channel). A swap the slicer, a macro or auto-refill
starts now shows on the IFS screen and in the Print Status card like
one started from the screen: the action and its step (a swap or a
refill shows Heat, Cut, Retract, then Feed and Purge), a translated
line such as "Swap to Slot 3 · Cutting filament" in place of the fixed
"IFS: loading", the target slot and the slot moving pulsing, and the
moving slot in the header. A lane-only move (pre-feed, tune, select)
shows as Selecting with no toolhead steps.

While the driver runs an operation the action stays busy, also between
its moves, so the runout check stays quiet through a refill or swap;
the 90 s action timeout and the head-sensor snap to idle leave the
driver's operation alone, as the driver reports its own end. A runout
raised on a paused print is dropped when the driver starts changing
the filament; an operation that ends with the print paused and the
toolhead empty arms the runout check again. Operations started from
the screen keep the phase tracker's steps.

An older driver without these fields keeps the plain activity mapping
(homing and selecting now show as Selecting).

Upstream: not applicable (AD5X OS specific)
---
diff --git a/include/ams_backend_ad5x_ifs.h b/include/ams_backend_ad5x_ifs.h
index 705aa6a..2e80112 100644
